 **Parameters and Edge Cases:**
-*   **Vicinity Size:** The size of the cuboid region queried for average density affects accuracy; if density values vary significantly within the vicinity, the assigned opacity may differ from the real one, causing artifacts [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Density Variability:** If density values vary significantly within the vicinity region, the average density may not accurately represent the local opacity, leading to artifacts [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Transfer Function Changes:** Since DSAT stores density, not opacity, changing the transfer function does not require recomputing the DSAT. The average density of the vicinity region remains constant, though the opacity used to estimate occlusion changes [S2, unofficial].
